      "DESCRIPTION": "FIND: bench/immune_agents.py, run_immune_pipeline(), Stage 3b Regulatory T section after reconciliation. The code computes pure v1 synthesis into `final_verdicts/final_confidences`, computes v2 into `v2_final/v2_conf`, then reconciles and overwrites `final_verdicts/final_confidences` with the merged result. After that overwrite, it calls `regulatory_t_cell_check(final_verdicts, triaged, max_rejection_rate)` and labels the result `v1_autoimmune`. That is not a v1 check; it is a check over reconciled outputs. Evidence from the function order: `helper_t_cell_synthesize(...)` -> `helper_t_v2_shadow(...)` -> `_reconciliation_gate(...)` -> `final_verdicts = reconciled_verdicts` -> `v1_autoimmune, v1_reg_reason = regulatory_t_cell_check(final_verdicts, ...)`. This invalidates the claimed 'v1 vs v2' comparison and can hide divergence between the actual v1 and v2 regulatory behavior.",
      "PROPOSED_FIX": "FIX: preserve pre-reconciliation v1 outputs and feed those into the v1 regulatory check.\n\n<<<<\n    # ── Stage 3a: Helper T v1 synthesis (kept for reconciliation) ────\n    t0 = time.monotonic()\n    final_verdicts, final_confidences = helper_t_cell_synthesize(triaged, all_verdicts)\n    timings[\"helper_t\"] = round(time.monotonic() - t0, 4)\n\n    # ── Stage 3a': Helper T v2 synthesis (WP6a: active) ──────────────\n    t0 = time.monotonic()\n    v2_final, v2_conf = helper_t_v2_shadow(triaged, all_verdicts)\n    timings[\"helper_t_v2\"] = round(time.monotonic() - t0, 4)\n\n    # ── Stage 3a.5: RECONCILIATION GATE (WP3b) ──────────────────────\n    # Immutable state transition check: once a finding is rejected/confirmed\n    # by both v1 and v2, that verdict is locked. Prevents autoimmune recovery\n    # from rescuing known garbage (MF-34/MF-35/C5-25).\n    t0 = time.monotonic()\n    reconciled_verdicts, reconciled_confidences = _reconciliation_gate(\n        final_verdicts, final_confidences, v2_final, v2_conf,\n    )\n    timings[\"reconciliation_gate\"] = round(time.monotonic() - t0, 4)\n\n    # Use reconciled verdicts for downstream processing\n    final_verdicts = reconciled_verdicts\n    final_confidences = reconciled_confidences\n\n    # ── Stage 3b: Regulatory T-Cell meta-check (WP6a: v2 primary) ────\n    t0 = time.monotonic()\n    v1_autoimmune, v1_reg_reason = regulatory_t_cell_check(\n        final_verdicts, triaged, max_rejection_rate,\n    )\n    v2_autoimmune, v2_reg_reason = regulatory_t_v2_shadow(\n        final_verdicts, triaged, max_rejection_rate,\n    )\n====\n    # ── Stage 3a: Helper T v1 synthesis (kept for reconciliation) ────\n    t0 = time.monotonic()\n    v1_final, v1_conf = helper_t_cell_synthesize(triaged, all_verdicts)\n    timings[\"helper_t\"] = round(time.monotonic() - t0, 4)\n\n    # ── Stage 3a': Helper T v2 synthesis (WP6a: active) ──────────────\n    t0 = time.monotonic()\n    v2_final, v2_conf = helper_t_v2_shadow(triaged, all_verdicts)\n    timings[\"helper_t_v2\"] = round(time.monotonic() - t0, 4)\n\n    # ── Stage 3a.5: RECONCILIATION GATE (WP3b) ──────────────────────\n    # Immutable state transition check: once a finding is rejected/confirmed\n    # by both v1 and v2, that verdict is locked. Prevents autoimmune recovery\n    # from rescuing known garbage (MF-34/MF-35/C5-25).\n    t0 = time.monotonic()\n    reconciled_verdicts, reconciled_confidences = _reconciliation_gate(\n        v1_final, v1_conf, v2_final, v2_conf,\n    )\n    timings[\"reconciliation_gate\"] = round(time.monotonic() - t0, 4)\n\n    # ── Stage 3b: Regulatory T-Cell meta-check (WP6a: v2 primary) ────\n    t0 = time.monotonic()\n    v1_autoimmune, v1_reg_reason = regulatory_t_cell_check(\n        v1_final, triaged, max_rejection_rate,\n    )\n    v2_autoimmune, v2_reg_reason = regulatory_t_v2_shadow(\n        reconciled_verdicts, triaged, max_rejection_rate,\n    )\n\n    # Use reconciled verdicts for downstream processing\n    final_verdicts = reconciled_verdicts\n    final_confidences = reconciled_confidences\n>>>>",
