      "DESCRIPTION": "FIND: bench/verification_chain.py, build_inclusion_proof() and verify_inclusion_proof(). `build_inclusion_proof()` always builds the proof against all current records and returns a freshly computed current root, while `verify_inclusion_proof()` accepts any caller-supplied `merkle_root`. This makes epoch sealing semantically meaningless for proofs: after additional appends, the same record's proof is no longer tied to the epoch root that allegedly sealed it. Evidence: sealed epochs are stored in `self._epochs` with `record_count` and `merkle_root`, but `build_inclusion_proof()` ignores epochs entirely and computes over `self._records`; there is no API to build a proof against a chosen epoch boundary.",
      "PROPOSED_FIX": "FIX: make inclusion proofs epoch-scoped and verify against the proof's own epoch metadata.\n\n<<<<\n    def build_inclusion_proof(self, index: int) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Build an RFC 9162 inclusion proof for the record at `index`.\"\"\"\n        if not (0 <= index < len(self._records)):\n            raise IndexError(\n                f\"Index {index} out of range [0, {len(self._records)})\"\n            )\n        leaves = [_digest_bytes(r[\"chain_hash\"]) for r in self._records]\n        proof_steps = rfc9162_inclusion_proof(leaves, index)\n        root = rfc9162_merkle_root(leaves)\n        return {\n            \"index\": index,\n            \"chain_hash\": self._records[index][\"chain_hash\"],\n            \"proof\": proof_steps,\n            \"merkle_root\": \"sha256:\" + root.hex(),\n        }\n\n    def verify_inclusion_proof(self, proof: dict, merkle_root: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Verify an inclusion proof against a given Merkle root.\n\n        merkle_root should be in 'sha256:<hex>' format.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            leaf_data = _digest_bytes(proof[\"chain_hash\"])\n            root_bytes = _digest_bytes(merkle_root)\n            return rfc9162_verify_inclusion(leaf_data, proof[\"proof\"], root_bytes)\n        except (KeyError, ValueError, TypeError):\n            return False\n====\n    def build_inclusion_proof(self, index: int, epoch_index: Optional[int] = None) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Build an RFC 9162 inclusion proof for the record at `index`.\n\n        If epoch_index is provided, the proof is built against that sealed epoch.\n        Otherwise, it is built against the latest sealed epoch containing the record.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not (0 <= index < len(self._records)):\n            raise IndexError(\n                f\"Index {index} out of range [0, {len(self._records)})\"\n            )\n        if not self._epochs:\n            raise ValueError(\"Cannot build inclusion proof without a sealed epoch\")\n\n        if epoch_index is None:\n            candidate_epochs = [e for e in self._epochs if index < e[\"record_count\"]]\n            if not candidate_epochs:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Record {index} is not included in any sealed epoch\")\n            epoch = candidate_epochs[0]\n        else:\n            if not (0 <= epoch_index < len(self._epochs)):\n                raise IndexError(\n                    f\"Epoch index {epoch_index} out of range [0, {len(self._epochs)})\"\n                )\n            epoch = self._epochs[epoch_index]\n            if index >= epoch[\"record_count\"]:\n                raise ValueError(\n                    f\"Record {index} is not included in sealed epoch {epoch_index}\"\n                )\n\n        leaves = [_digest_bytes(r[\"chain_hash\"]) for r in self._records[:epoch[\"record_count\"]]]\n        proof_steps = rfc9162_inclusion_proof(leaves, index)\n        root = rfc9162_merkle_root(leaves)\n        return {\n            \"index\": index,\n            \"epoch_index\": epoch[\"epoch_index\"],\n            \"record_count\": epoch[\"record_count\"],\n            \"chain_hash\": self._records[index][\"chain_hash\"],\n            \"proof\": proof_steps,\n            \"merkle_root\": \"sha256:\" + root.hex(),\n        }\n\n    def verify_inclusion_proof(self, proof: dict, merkle_root: Optional[str] = None) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Verify an inclusion proof against an explicit or embedded Merkle root.\n\n        If merkle_root is None, uses proof['merkle_root'].\n        Root must be in 'sha256:<hex>' format.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            leaf_data = _digest_bytes(proof[\"chain_hash\"])\n            root_str = merkle_root if merkle_root is not None else proof[\"merkle_root\"]\n            root_bytes = _digest_bytes(root_str)\n            return rfc9162_verify_inclusion(leaf_data, proof[\"proof\"], root_bytes)\n        except (KeyError, ValueError, TypeError):\n            return False\n>>>>",
