    "DESCRIPTION": "FIND: `bench/immune_agents.py`, interaction between `cytotoxic_t_cell()`, `cytotoxic_t_cell_v2_shadow()`, `b_cell_verify()`, `b_cell_v2_shadow()`, and `helper_t_cell_synthesize()`. The v1 helper deduplicates verdicts by `CellType` only, but both v1 and v2 implementations reuse the same enum values (`CellType.CYTOTOXIC_T` and `CellType.B_CELL`). Evidence: `helper_t_cell_synthesize()` builds `seen_cells: Dict[CellType, CellVerdict]` and keeps only the highest-confidence verdict per cell type per finding. Since CT v1 and CT v2 both emit `cell_type=CellType.CYTOTOXIC_T`, and B-cell v1/v2 both emit `cell_type=CellType.B_CELL`, one pipeline's output can erase the other's before v1 synthesis. In the active Run 11/12 path, this means the allegedly independent v2 signals are not actually independent in helper v1; the higher-confidence one silently dominates. This undermines the stated dual-pipeline architecture and also contaminates reconciliation, because `final_verdicts` from helper v1 are already missing one side of the evidence base.",
    "PROPOSED_FIX": "FIX:\n\n<<<<\nclass CellType(Enum):\n    \"\"\"Immune cell types mapped to verification roles.\"\"\"\n    DENDRITIC = \"dendritic\"\n    CYTOTOXIC_T = \"cytotoxic_t\"\n    B_CELL = \"b_cell\"\n    NK_CELL = \"nk_cell\"\n    HELPER_T = \"helper_t\"\n    REGULATORY_T = \"regulatory_t\"\n====\nclass CellType(Enum):\n    \"\"\"Immune cell types mapped to verification roles.\"\"\"\n    DENDRITIC = \"dendritic\"\n    CYTOTOXIC_T = \"cytotoxic_t\"\n    CYTOTOXIC_T_V2 = \"cytotoxic_t_v2\"\n    B_CELL = \"b_cell\"\n    B_CELL_V2 = \"b_cell_v2\"\n    NK_CELL = \"nk_cell\"\n    HELPER_T = \"helper_t\"\n    REGULATORY_T = \"regulatory_t\"\n>>>>\n\n<<<<\n            verdicts.append(CellVerdict(\n                cell_type=CellType.CYTOTOXIC_T,\n                finding_id=fid,\n                verdict=std_verdict,\n====\n            verdicts.append(CellVerdict(\n                cell_type=CellType.CYTOTOXIC_T_V2,\n                finding_id=fid,\n                verdict=std_verdict,\n>>>>\n\n<<<<\n                verdicts.append(CellVerdict(\n                    cell_type=CellType.CYTOTOXIC_T,\n                    finding_id=fid,\n                    verdict=\"UNCERTAIN\",\n====\n                verdicts.append(CellVerdict(\n                    cell_type=CellType.CYTOTOXIC_T_V2,\n                    finding_id=fid,\n                    verdict=\"UNCERTAIN\",\n>>>>\n\n<<<<\n        return CellVerdict(\n            cell_type=CellType.B_CELL, finding_id=\"\",\n            verdict=\"UNCERTAIN\", confidence=0.15,\n====\n        return CellVerdict(\n            cell_type=CellType.B_CELL_V2, finding_id=\"\",\n            verdict=\"UNCERTAIN\", confidence=0.15,\n>>>>\n\n<<<<\n        return CellVerdict(\n            cell_type=CellType.B_CELL, finding_id=\"\",\n            verdict=\"CONFIRMED\", confidence=0.85,\n====\n        return CellVerdict(\n            cell_type=CellType.B_CELL_V2, finding_id=\"\",\n            verdict=\"CONFIRMED\", confidence=0.85,\n>>>>\n\n<<<<\n        return CellVerdict(\n            cell_type=CellType.B_CELL, finding_id=\"\",\n            verdict=\"REJECTED\", confidence=0.85,\n====\n        return CellVerdict(\n            cell_type=CellType.B_CELL_V2, finding_id=\"\",\n            verdict=\"REJECTED\", confidence=0.85,\n>>>>\n\n<<<<\n        return CellVerdict(\n            cell_type=CellType.B_CELL, finding_id=\"\",\n            verdict=\"UNCERTAIN\", confidence=0.20,\n====\n        return CellVerdict(\n            cell_type=CellType.B_CELL_V2, finding_id=\"\",\n            verdict=\"UNCERTAIN\", confidence=0.20,\n>>>>",
    "VERIFIED": true,
    "FOLLOW": "After this change, `helper_t_cell_synthesize()` will preserve one verdict per actual pipeline component instead of one per coarse family, so CT v1 and CT v2 can both contribute. `_verdict_domain()` in helper v2 already classifies by `tool_used` substrings, so it does not need changes for domain grouping. Any code that compares exact enum membership must be checked: `formalisation_agent_shadow()` filters by `v.cell_type == CellType.B_CELL`, so after the enum split it still intentionally targets only v1 B-cell verdicts, which is consistent with its current purpose. Logging and serialization via enum `.value` continue to work. This fix also strengthens ChatGPT's F061 concern: once dedup and v2 evidence are preserved distinctly, concurrent scheduling artifacts become more visible rather than being masked by cell-type collapse."
