    "DESCRIPTION": "FIND: `bench/immune_agents.py`, function `formalisation_agent_shadow()`. The lookup of B-cell verdicts by finding ID overwrites earlier verdicts with later ones from any B-cell-family source because it keys only by `finding_id` and filters only on `v.cell_type == CellType.B_CELL`. In the current artifact, both `_verify_z3_v2_shadow()` and v1 B-cell emit `CellType.B_CELL`, so the dict assignment `bcell_verdicts[v.finding_id] = v` can replace the real v1 verdict with the v2 shadow verdict depending on completion order in `all_verdicts`. Evidence: `run_immune_pipeline()` collects futures in order `b_cell` then `b_cell_v2`, so later B-cell-v2 verdicts deterministically overwrite earlier v1 verdicts in `formalisation_agent_shadow()`. The function's comments explicitly say it compares against 'the B-Cell's verdict' to detect false rejections from context erasure, but it can instead inspect the wrong verifier family. This is a concrete downstream corruption caused by the shared cell type and naive lookup logic.",
    "PROPOSED_FIX": "FIX:\n\n<<<<\n    # Build B-Cell verdict lookup\n    bcell_verdicts: Dict[str, CellVerdict] = {}\n    for v in b_cell_verdicts:\n        if v.cell_type == CellType.B_CELL:\n            bcell_verdicts[v.finding_id] = v\n====\n    # Build B-Cell v1 verdict lookup only\n    bcell_verdicts: Dict[str, CellVerdict] = {}\n    for v in b_cell_verdicts:\n        if v.tool_used in (\"sympy\", \"z3\", \"statsmodels\"):\n            bcell_verdicts[v.finding_id] = v\n>>>>",
    "VERIFIED": true,
