    "description": "FIND: bench/immune_agents.py, function run_immune_pipeline(), Stage 2 NK collection and downstream synthesis/filtering. NK v2 is configured as the active primary dedup path, but the pipeline drops the updated TriagedFinding state returned by nk_cell_v2_shadow(). The code submits `nk_cell_v2_shadow(triaged_for_nk, ...)`, then collects only `_, nk_verdicts = result` and never copies `is_duplicate`, `duplicate_of`, or `similarity` back into the main `triaged` list used by B-cell/Helper T/filtering. Evidence: helper_t_cell_synthesize() only hard-auto-rejects duplicates when `tf.is_duplicate` is true; otherwise DUPLICATE is merely accumulated as reject weight. Evidence also in run_immune_pipeline() final filtering: it iterates over `triaged`, not the NK-mutated copy. So activated NK v2 dedup can fail to enforce duplicate semantics on the main pipeline state.\n\nFIX:\n<<<<\n        for name, future in futures.items():\n            try:\n                result = future.result(timeout=ct_timeout + 30)\n                if name == \"nk_v2\":\n                    # NK v2 returns (triaged, verdicts) tuple\n                    _, nk_verdicts = result\n                    all_verdicts.extend(nk_verdicts)\n                    for v in nk_verdicts:\n                        tool_usage[v.tool_used] = tool_usage.get(v.tool_used, 0) + 1\n                else:\n                    cell_verdicts = result\n                    all_verdicts.extend(cell_verdicts)\n                    for v in cell_verdicts:\n                        tool_usage[v.tool_used] = tool_usage.get(v.tool_used, 0) + 1\n            except Exception as e:\n====\n        for name, future in futures.items():\n            try:\n                result = future.result(timeout=ct_timeout + 30)\n                if name == \"nk_v2\":\n                    # NK v2 returns (triaged, verdicts) tuple\n                    nk_triaged, nk_verdicts = result\n                    nk_by_id = {tf.finding.finding_id: tf for tf in nk_triaged}\n                    for tf in triaged:\n                        nk_tf = nk_by_id.get(tf.finding.finding_id)\n                        if nk_tf is not None:\n                            tf.is_duplicate = nk_tf.is_duplicate\n                            tf.duplicate_of = nk_tf.duplicate_of\n                            tf.similarity = nk_tf.similarity\n                    all_verdicts.extend(nk_verdicts)\n                    for v in nk_verdicts:\n                        tool_usage[v.tool_used] = tool_usage.get(v.tool_used, 0) + 1\n                else:\n                    cell_verdicts = result\n                    all_verdicts.extend(cell_verdicts)\n                    for v in cell_verdicts:\n                        tool_usage[v.tool_used] = tool_usage.get(v.tool_used, 0) + 1\n            except Exception as e:\n>>>>\n\nFOLLOW: This fix changes behavior in helper_t_cell_synthesize(), helper_t_v2_shadow(), and the final filtered/rejected partition in run_immune_pipeline(), because those functions read `tf.is_duplicate` from the main `triaged` list. After propagation, duplicates become hard DUPLICATE outcomes again instead of soft reject-weight evidence. It also means B-cell/Formalisation/Regulatory stages now evaluate the same triaged identity set as NK, eliminating state divergence between `triaged` and `triaged_for_nk`. No additional interface changes are required because nk_cell_v2_shadow() already returns the needed tuple."
  },
