    "abstraction_index": 0.62,
    "description": "FIND: bench/immune_agents.py, function regulatory_t_cell_check(), Check 3 'All findings from one model rejected'. The implementation counts only `REJECTED`, but the pipeline's own removal semantics treat both `REJECTED` and `DUPLICATE` as removed. Evidence: the same function computes `duplicated`, `removed = rejected + duplicated`, and `removal_rate = removed / total`, explicitly acknowledging duplicates as removals. Later, run_immune_pipeline() computes `rej_count = sum(1 for v in final_verdicts.values() if v in (\"REJECTED\", \"DUPLICATE\"))`. But model-bias check ignores DUPLICATE, so a model can have every finding removed as duplicates without triggering the systematic-bias guard. That is an internal inconsistency in the autoimmune logic.\n\nFIX:\n<<<<\n    model_counts: Dict[str, int] = {}\n    model_rejected: Dict[str, int] = {}\n    for tf in triaged:\n        mid = tf.finding.model_id\n        model_counts[mid] = model_counts.get(mid, 0) + 1\n        if final_verdicts.get(tf.finding.finding_id) == \"REJECTED\":\n            model_rejected[mid] = model_rejected.get(mid, 0) + 1\n\n    for mid, total_m in model_counts.items():\n        rej_m = model_rejected.get(mid, 0)\n        if total_m >= 3 and rej_m == total_m:\n            reasons.append(\n                f\"All {total_m} findings from {mid} rejected — \"\n                f\"possible systematic bias against this model\"\n            )\n====\n    model_counts: Dict[str, int] = {}\n    model_removed: Dict[str, int] = {}\n    for tf in triaged:\n        mid = tf.finding.model_id\n        model_counts[mid] = model_counts.get(mid, 0) + 1\n        if final_verdicts.get(tf.finding.finding_id) in (\"REJECTED\", \"DUPLICATE\"):\n            model_removed[mid] = model_removed.get(mid, 0) + 1\n\n    for mid, total_m in model_counts.items():\n        rem_m = model_removed.get(mid, 0)\n        if total_m >= 3 and rem_m == total_m:\n            reasons.append(\n                f\"All {total_m} findings from {mid} removed (REJECTED/DUPLICATE) — \"\n                f\"possible systematic bias against this model\"\n            )\n>>>>\n\nFOLLOW: This fix makes v1 Regulatory T semantics consistent with run_immune_pipeline() rejection-rate accounting and with regulatory_t_v2_shadow(), which already reasons in terms of removal. It also narrows an otherwise misleading v1 vs v2 comparison log in run_immune_pipeline(): after the fix, disagreements between `v1_autoimmune` and `v2_autoimmune` become more likely to reflect the proportional-threshold change, not a category mismatch on duplicates."
