    "abstraction_index": 0.81,
    "description": "FIND: bench/immune_agents.py, function _reconciliation_gate(). The gate claims immutable-state protection and 'REJECTED verdicts from both pipelines are LOCKED', but the implementation is just generic max-confidence merging and has no lock logic. More importantly, it treats UNCERTAIN as a normal competing verdict. Evidence: if v1=CONFIRMED(0.40) and v2=UNCERTAIN(0.90), the code chooses UNCERTAIN because v2c > v1c. That allows an uncertain shadow/secondary path to override affirmative evidence, contradicting the stated purpose of reconciliation before Regulatory T. This is a new downstream flaw exposed by F003 but exists independently in the current code.\n\nFIX:\n<<<<\n    all_fids = set(v1_verdicts) | set(v2_verdicts)\n    for fid in all_fids:\n        v1v = v1_verdicts.get(fid)\n        v1c = v1_confidences.get(fid, 0.0)\n        v2v = v2_verdicts.get(fid)\n        v2c = v2_confidences.get(fid, 0.0)\n\n        if v1v is None and v2v is not None:\n            reconciled[fid] = v2v\n            reconciled_conf[fid] = v2c\n        elif v2v is None and v1v is not None:\n            reconciled[fid] = v1v\n            reconciled_conf[fid] = v1c\n        elif v1v == v2v:\n            # Agreement: use shared verdict, max confidence\n            reconciled[fid] = v1v\n            reconciled_conf[fid] = max(v1c, v2c)\n        else:\n            # Disagreement: higher confidence wins\n            if v1c >= v2c:\n                reconciled[fid] = v1v\n                reconciled_conf[fid] = v1c\n            else:\n                reconciled[fid] = v2v\n                reconciled_conf[fid] = v2c\n====\n    all_fids = set(v1_verdicts) | set(v2_verdicts)\n    for fid in all_fids:\n        v1v = v1_verdicts.get(fid)\n        v1c = v1_confidences.get(fid, 0.0)\n        v2v = v2_verdicts.get(fid)\n        v2c = v2_confidences.get(fid, 0.0)\n\n        if v1v is None and v2v is not None:\n            reconciled[fid] = v2v\n            reconciled_conf[fid] = v2c\n        elif v2v is None and v1v is not None:\n            reconciled[fid] = v1v\n            reconciled_conf[fid] = v1c\n        elif v1v == \"REJECTED\" and v2v == \"REJECTED\":\n            reconciled[fid] = \"REJECTED\"\n            reconciled_conf[fid] = max(v1c, v2c)\n        elif v1v == v2v:\n            reconciled[fid] = v1v\n            reconciled_conf[fid] = max(v1c, v2c)\n        elif v1v == \"UNCERTAIN\" and v2v != \"UNCERTAIN\":\n            reconciled[fid] = v2v\n            reconciled_conf[fid] = v2c\n        elif v2v == \"UNCERTAIN\" and v1v != \"UNCERTAIN\":\n            reconciled[fid] = v1v\n            reconciled_conf[fid] = v1c\n        else:\n            if v1c >= v2c:\n                reconciled[fid] = v1v\n                reconciled_conf[fid] = v1c\n            else:\n                reconciled[fid] = v2v\n                reconciled_conf[fid] = v2c\n>>>>\n\nFOLLOW: This alters downstream final_verdicts passed into regulatory_t_cell_check(), regulatory_t_v2_shadow(), and final filtered/rejected partitioning in run_immune_pipeline(). In particular, autoimmune behavior will now be driven by substantive CONFIRMED/REJECTED disagreements instead of high-confidence UNCERTAIN placeholders overriding them. It also makes the docstring's lock claim partially true for dual REJECTED cases; if full lock semantics for CONFIRMED/DUPLICATE are desired, the docstring should be narrowed or the lock set expanded."
