      "DESCRIPTION": "FIND: bench/immune_agents.py, function run_immune_pipeline(), Stage 0/response build. Findings rejected by the active skin barrier are removed from new_findings when observation_only is False, but they are never added to the returned rejected_findings list. Evidence: barrier_rejected is computed, then ignored; later rejected is rebuilt only from triaged findings, and triaged no longer contains barrier-failed findings. Result: callers cannot observe which findings were filtered by the deterministic pre-filter, and rejection accounting is incomplete.",
      "PROPOSED_FIX": "FIX:\n<<<<\n    filtered: List[Finding] = []\n    rejected: List[Finding] = []\n\n    for tf in triaged:\n        fid = tf.finding.finding_id\n        verdict = final_verdicts.get(fid, \"UNCERTAIN\")\n\n        if observation_only:\n            # Observation mode: everything passes through\n            filtered.append(tf.finding)\n        elif verdict in (\"CONFIRMED\", \"UNCERTAIN\"):\n            filtered.append(tf.finding)\n        else:\n            rejected.append(tf.finding)\n\n    # If autoimmune flagged, override: pass everything through\n    if autoimmune_flag and not observation_only:\n        filtered = [tf.finding for tf in triaged]\n        rejected = []\n====\n    filtered: List[Finding] = []\n    rejected: List[Finding] = list(barrier_rejected)\n\n    for tf in triaged:\n        fid = tf.finding.finding_id\n        verdict = final_verdicts.get(fid, \"UNCERTAIN\")\n\n        if observation_only:\n            # Observation mode: everything passes through\n            filtered.append(tf.finding)\n        elif verdict in (\"CONFIRMED\", \"UNCERTAIN\"):\n            filtered.append(tf.finding)\n        else:\n            rejected.append(tf.finding)\n\n    # If autoimmune flagged, override only pipeline-stage rejections.\n    # Skin barrier failures remain rejected because they failed a deterministic\n    # precondition check before immune synthesis.\n    if autoimmune_flag and not observation_only:\n        filtered = [tf.finding for tf in triaged]\n        rejected = list(barrier_rejected)\n>>>>",
