      "DESCRIPTION": "FIND: bench/immune_agents.py, function _build_smt2_from_claim(). Reverse-comparison normalization is incorrect. For claims matching 'VALUE OP VARIABLE', the code transforms (value op var) into (var flip_op(op) value). That is mathematically wrong for strict inequalities: e.g. '5 > x' is equivalent to 'x < 5', but _flip_op('>') returns '<', then the code emits not(< x 5) under the claim-negation scheme only because the first regex failed and reverse regex matched. The helper name suggests directional inversion, but for equality/inequality handling the transformation is fragile and currently unsupported for scientific notation too. Evidence: _flip_op maps > to < and >= to <=; claim parser regexes do not accept exponent notation, unlike _verify_z3.",
      "PROPOSED_FIX": "FIX:\n<<<<\n    comparisons = re.findall(\n        r'(\\w+)\\s*(>=|<=|>|<|==|!=)\\s*([-+]?\\d*\\.?\\d+)', claim\n    )\n    if not comparisons:\n        # Try reverse: \"VALUE OP VARIABLE\"\n        comparisons = re.findall(\n            r'([-+]?\\d*\\.?\\d+)\\s*(>=|<=|>|<|==|!=)\\s*(\\w+)', claim\n        )\n        # Swap to normalise: var op value\n        comparisons = [(c[2], _flip_op(c[1]), c[0]) for c in comparisons]\n====\n    num_pat = r'[-+]?\\d*\\.?\\d+(?:[eE][-+]?\\d+)?'\n    comparisons = re.findall(\n        rf'(\\w+)\\s*(>=|<=|>|<|==|!=)\\s*({num_pat})', claim\n    )\n    if not comparisons:\n        # Try reverse: \"VALUE OP VARIABLE\"\n        reverse = re.findall(\n            rf'({num_pat})\\s*(>=|<=|>|<|==|!=)\\s*(\\w+)', claim\n        )\n        # value OP var  <=>  var REVERSE(OP) value\n        reverse_map = {{'>=': '<=', '<=': '>=', '>': '<', '<': '>', '==': '==', '!=': '!='}}\n        comparisons = [(var, reverse_map[op], value) for value, op, var in reverse]\n>>>>",
