    "PROPOSED_FIX": "FIX: preserve the original input list and include barrier-filtered findings in the autoimmune override, or explicitly narrow the comment/policy. Exact code replacement for full override semantics:\n<<<<\ndef run_immune_pipeline(\n    new_findings: List[Finding],\n    prior_findings: List[Finding],\n    source_paths: List[str],\n    observation_only: bool = True,\n    ct_enabled: bool = True,\n    ct_timeout: int = 180,\n    tau_sim: float = 0.33,  # Calibrated from Run 8: max sim 0.553 at old 0.8\n    false_positive_db: Optional[List[Dict[str, Any]]] = None,\n    max_rejection_rate: float = 0.50,\n) -> ImmuneResponse:\n====\ndef run_immune_pipeline(\n    new_findings: List[Finding],\n    prior_findings: List[Finding],\n    source_paths: List[str],\n    observation_only: bool = True,\n    ct_enabled: bool = True,\n    ct_timeout: int = 180,\n    tau_sim: float = 0.33,  # Calibrated from Run 8: max sim 0.553 at old 0.8\n    false_positive_db: Optional[List[Dict[str, Any]]] = None,\n    max_rejection_rate: float = 0.50,\n) -> ImmuneResponse:\n>>>>\nAnd inside the function:\n<<<<\n    timings: Dict[str, float] = {}\n    tool_usage: Dict[str, int] = {}\n====\n    timings: Dict[str, float] = {}\n    tool_usage: Dict[str, int] = {}\n    original_findings = list(new_findings)\n>>>>\nAnd final override block:\n<<<<\n    # If autoimmune flagged, override: pass everything through\n    if autoimmune_flag and not observation_only:\n        filtered = [tf.finding for tf in triaged]\n        rejected = []\n====\n    # If autoimmune flagged, override: pass the original round input through,\n    # including any findings filtered earlier by the skin barrier.\n    if autoimmune_flag and not observation_only:\n        filtered = list(original_findings)\n        rejected = []\n>>>>",
