    "DESCRIPTION": "FIND: `bench/verification_chain.py`, methods `save_json()` and `load_json()`. Persistence round-tripping is not schema-preserving for signed chains because signer identity material is discarded on save and cannot be reconstructed on load. Evidence: `append_record()` emits `signature.key_id` and base64 signature per record, but the chain object's signer/verifier configuration is not serialized anywhere; `load_json()` always constructs `chain = cls()` with no signer. After load, appending new records to a previously signed chain silently produces `claimed_only` records, creating a mixed-authentication chain without explicit transition. Prior models noted signer state loss in broad terms; the deeper persistence-layer flaw is that the format provides no chain-level signing policy field, so a loaded chain cannot even detect the transition before the next append.",
    "PROPOSED_FIX": "FIX: persist an explicit chain-level signing policy and reject appends that would downgrade authentication after load unless a signer is reattached. Exact replacements:\n<<<<\n    def __init__(self, signer: Optional[Signer] = None):\n        self._records: list[dict] = []\n        self._epochs: list[dict] = []\n        self._signer = signer\n        self._schema_version = SCHEMA_VERSION\n====\n    def __init__(self, signer: Optional[Signer] = None):\n        self._records: list[dict] = []\n        self._epochs: list[dict] = []\n        self._signer = signer\n        self._schema_version = SCHEMA_VERSION\n        self._requires_authenticated_appends = signer is not None\n>>>>\n<<<<\n        data = {\n            \"schema_version\": self._schema_version,\n            \"records\": self._records,\n            \"epochs\": self._epochs,\n        }\n====\n        data = {\n            \"schema_version\": self._schema_version,\n            \"requires_authenticated_appends\": self._requires_authenticated_appends,\n            \"records\": self._records,\n            \"epochs\": self._epochs,\n        }\n>>>>\n<<<<\n        chain = cls()\n        chain._schema_version = data.get(\"schema_version\", SCHEMA_VERSION)\n        chain._records = data.get(\"records\", [])\n        chain._epochs = data.get(\"epochs\", [])\n        return chain\n====\n        chain = cls()\n        chain._schema_version = data.get(\"schema_version\", SCHEMA_VERSION)\n        chain._requires_authenticated_appends = data.get(\n            \"requires_authenticated_appends\",\n            any(r.get(\"signature\", {}).get(\"attribution\") == \"authenticated\"\n                for r in data.get(\"records\", []))\n        )\n        chain._records = data.get(\"records\", [])\n        chain._epochs = data.get(\"epochs\", [])\n        return chain\n>>>>\nAnd guard append:\n<<<<\n        seq = len(self._records)\n====\n        if self._requires_authenticated_appends and self._signer is None