    "DESCRIPTION": "FIND: `bench/immune_agents.py`, function `_build_smt2_from_claim()`. Duplicate negated assertions for the same grounded variable are appended once per comparison, causing redundant or contradictory formulas and needlessly inflating SMT size. Evidence: for a claim like `x > 1 and x > 2`, the loop emits one declaration, one grounding assert, and two separate negated claim asserts. That may be semantically acceptable, but for repeated or mixed comparisons on the same variable it can create multiple independent negations instead of a single negation of the combined claim, which changes the intended proof target from `not(claim)` to `not(c1) and not(c2) ...`. Prior models identified logical unsat in multi-condition cases; the missed implementation-level consequence is unnecessary formula growth and incorrect conjunction semantics even for otherwise parseable grounded claims.",
    "PROPOSED_FIX": "FIX: accumulate per-comparison predicates and negate their conjunction once. Exact replacement:\n<<<<\n    declarations: List[str] = []\n    assertions: List[str] = []\n    has_grounding = False\n\n    for var_name, op, value_str in comparisons:\n        try:\n            value = float(value_str)\n        except ValueError:\n            continue\n\n        # Declare each variable only once (SMT-LIB rejects duplicates)\n        if var_name not in declared:\n            declarations.append(f\"(declare-const {var_name} Real)\")\n            declared.add(var_name)\n\n        smt_op = {\">=\": \">=\", \"<=\": \"<=\", \">\": \">\", \"<\": \"<\",\n                   \"==\": \"=\", \"!=\": \"distinct\"}[op]\n\n        # Check if this variable has a grounded value from the AST\n        if var_name in constants and isinstance(constants[var_name], (int, float)):\n            grounded = float(constants[var_name])\n            # Assert the grounded value (only once per variable)\n            grounding_assert = f\"(assert (= {var_name} {grounded}))\"\n            if grounding_assert not in assertions:\n                assertions.append(grounding_assert)\n            # Assert the negation of the claim (to check via UNSAT)\n            assertions.append(\n                f\"(assert (not ({smt_op} {var_name} {value})))\"\n            )\n            has_grounding = True\n        else:\n            # Ungrounded variable — can only build abstract proof\n            assertions.append(\n                f\"(assert (not ({smt_op} {var_name} {value})))\"\n            )\n\n    if not assertions:\n        return None\n\n    smt2 = \"\\n\".join(declarations + assertions + [\"(check-sat)\"])\n    return smt2 if has_grounding else None  # Only return if grounded\n====\n    declarations: List[str] = []\n    grounding_assertions: List[str] = []\n    predicates: List[str] = []\n    has_grounding = False\n\n    for var_name, op, value_str in comparisons:\n        try:\n            value = float(value_str)\n        except ValueError:\n            continue\n\n        if var_name not in declared:\n            declarations.append(f\"(declare-const {var_name} Real)\")\n            declared.add(var_name)\n\n        smt_op = {\">=\": \">=\", \"<=\": \"<=\", \">\": \">\", \"<\": \"<\",\n                  \"==\": \"=\", \"!=\": \"distinct\"}[op]\n        predicates.append(f\"({smt_op} {var_name} {value})\")\n\n        if var_name in constants and isinstance(constants[var_name], (int, float)):\n            grounded = float(constants[var_name])\n            grounding_assert = f\"(assert (= {var_name} {grounded}))\"\n            if grounding_assert not in grounding_assertions:\n                grounding_assertions.append(grounding_assert)\n            has_grounding = True\n\n    if not predicates or not has_grounding:\n        return None\n\n    claim_expr = predicates[0] if len(predicates) == 1 else f\"(and {' '.join(predicates)})\"\n    smt2 = \"\\n\".join(\n        declarations + grounding_assertions + [f\"(assert (not {claim_expr}))\", \"(check-sat)\"]\n    )\n    return smt2\n>>>>",
