    "DESCRIPTION": "VerificationChain.verify_inclusion_proof() and the CLI proof verifier validate only the Merkle branch against a supplied root; they do not bind that proof to any epoch or verify that the root is actually sealed in the chain. A caller can present a valid proof for the current unsealed head state, or any arbitrary root they choose, and get a VALID result even though no epoch ever sealed that root. In a persistence layer whose stated guarantee is epoch inclusion over sealed epochs, this is a correctness gap: inclusion is being proven against an untrusted root, not against chain state.",
    "PROPOSED_FIX": "Require epoch binding in inclusion proofs and verify against stored sealed epochs. Include epoch_index and record_count in build_inclusion_proof(); add a verifier that checks the supplied merkle_root matches a stored epoch with that record_count before validating the branch. Update the CLI prove-record path to emit epoch-bound proofs and CLI verify-proof to reject proofs not anchored to a sealed epoch.",
    "VERIFIED": true,
    "FIND": "Location: bench/verification_chain.py, methods build_inclusion_proof(), verify_inclusion_proof(), and CLI handler _cli_verify_proof(). Evidence: build_inclusion_proof() always computes leaves over all current records and returns {index, chain_hash, proof, merkle_root}; it does not reference self._epochs at all. verify_inclusion_proof(proof, merkle_root) merely parses proof['chain_hash'], proof['proof'], and the caller-supplied merkle_root and calls rfc9162_verify_inclusion(). _cli_verify_proof() similarly accepts any --root, warns if it differs from proof['merkle_root'], and still verifies against the supplied root. Therefore a proof can validate against an unsealed snapshot root or an arbitrary externally supplied root. That is inconsistent with the module docstring claim: 'Epoch inclusion: RFC 9162-compliant Merkle trees over sealed epochs allow compact inclusion proofs for any individual record.'",
    "FIX": "<<<<\n    def build_inclusion_proof(self, index: int) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Build an RFC 9162 inclusion proof for the record at `index`.\"\"\"\n        if not (0 <= index < len(self._records)):\n            raise IndexError(\n                f\"Index {index} out of range [0, {len(self._records)})\"\n            )\n        leaves = [_digest_bytes(r[\"chain_hash\"]) for r in self._records]\n        proof_steps = rfc9162_inclusion_proof(leaves, index)\n        root = rfc9162_merkle_root(leaves)\n        return {\n            \"index\": index,\n            \"chain_hash\": self._records[index][\"chain_hash\"],\n            \"proof\": proof_steps,\n            \"merkle_root\": \"sha256:\" + root.hex(),\n        }\n\n    def verify_inclusion_proof(self, proof: dict, merkle_root: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Verify an inclusion proof against a given Merkle root.\n\n        merkle_root should be in 'sha256:<hex>' format.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            leaf_data = _digest_bytes(proof[\"chain_hash\"])\n            root_bytes = _digest_bytes(merkle_root)\n            return rfc9162_verify_inclusion(leaf_data, proof[\"proof\"], root_bytes)\n        except (KeyError, ValueError, TypeError):\n            return False\n====\n    def build_inclusion_proof(self, index: int, epoch_index: Optional[int] = None) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Build an RFC 9162 inclusion proof for the record at `index` bound to a sealed epoch.\"\"\"\n        if not (0 <= index < len(self._records)):\n            raise IndexError(\n                f\"Index {index} out of range [0, {len(self._records)})\"\n            )\n        if not self._epochs:\n            raise ValueError(\"Cannot build epoch inclusion proof: no sealed epochs exist\")\n\n        if epoch_index is None:\n            candidate_epochs = [e for e in self._epochs if index < e[\"record_count\"]]\n            if not candidate_epochs:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Record {index} is not included in any sealed epoch\")\n            epoch = candidate_epochs[-1]\n        else:\n            if not (0 <= epoch_index < len(self._epochs)):\n                raise IndexError(\n                    f\"Epoch index {epoch_index} out of range [0, {len(self._epochs)})\"\n                )\n            epoch = self._epochs[epoch_index]\n            if index >= epoch[\"record_count\"]:\n                raise ValueError(\n                    f\"Record {index} is not included in epoch {epoch_index} \"\n                    f\"with record_count={epoch['record_count']}\"\n                )\n\n        record_count = epoch[\"record_count\"]\n        leaves = [_digest_bytes(r[\"chain_hash\"]) for r in self._records[:record_count]]\n        proof_steps = rfc9162_inclusion_proof(leaves, index)\n        root = rfc9162_merkle_root(leaves)\n        return {\n            \"index\": index,\n            \"chain_hash\": self._records[index][\"chain_hash\"],\n            \"proof\": proof_steps,\n            \"epoch_index\": epoch[\"epoch_index\"],\n            \"record_count\": record_count,\n            \"merkle_root\": \"sha256:\" + root.hex(),\n        }\n\n    def verify_inclusion_proof(self, proof: dict, merkle_root: Optional[str] = None) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Verify an inclusion proof against a sealed epoch in this chain.\n\n        If merkle_root is provided, it must match both the proof and the stored epoch.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            epoch_index = proof[\"epoch_index\"]\n            record_count = proof[\"record_count\"]\n            if not (0 <= epoch_index < len(self._epochs)):\n                return False\n            epoch = self._epochs[epoch_index]\n            if epoch[\"record_count\"] != record_count:\n                return False\n            epoch_root = epoch[\"merkle_root\"]\n            if proof.get(\"merkle_root\") != epoch_root:\n                return False\n            if merkle_root is not None and merkle_root != epoch_root:\n                return False\n            leaf_data = _digest_bytes(proof[\"chain_hash\"])\n            root_bytes = _digest_bytes(epoch_root)\n            return rfc9162_verify_inclusion(leaf_data, proof[\"proof\"], root_bytes)\n        except (KeyError, ValueError, TypeError):\n            return False\n>>>>",
    "FOLLOW": "Downstream impact is mandatory in CLI. _cli_prove_record currently emits a proof for the live full chain, not a sealed epoch. It must either require an epoch selection or default to the latest epoch containing the record. Concrete fix:\n<<<<\n    proof = chain.build_inclusion_proof(args.index)\n====\n    proof = chain.build_inclusion_proof(args.index, epoch_index=getattr(args, \"epoch_index\", None))\n>>>>\nAlso _cli_verify_proof currently bypasses chain state entirely by calling rfc9162_verify_inclusion() directly. It must load the chain and delegate to chain.verify_inclusion_proof(), otherwise the new epoch binding is dead code. Concrete replacement:\n<<<<\ndef _cli_verify_proof(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Handle the 'verify-proof' subcommand.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        with open(args.proof_file, \"r\") as f:\n            proof = json.load(f)\n        # Accept both 'sha256:<hex>' and bare hex for the root\n        root_str = args.root\n        if root_str.startswith(\"sha256:\"):\n            root_bytes = bytes.fromhex(root_str[7:])\n        else:\n            root_bytes = bytes.fromhex(root_str)\n        # Warn if supplied root differs from proof's embedded root\n        if \"merkle_root\" in proof:\n            proof_root_hex = proof[\"merkle_root\"].replace(\"sha256:\", \"\")\n            supplied_hex = root_str.replace(\"sha256:\", \"\")\n            if proof_root_hex != supplied_hex:\n                print(\n                    \"WARNING: supplied root differs from proof's \"\n                    \"embedded merkle_root\",\n                    file=sys.stderr,\n                )\n        valid = rfc9162_verify_inclusion(\n            _digest_bytes(proof[\"chain_hash\"]),\n            proof[\"proof\"],\n            root_bytes,\n        )\n    except (KeyError, ValueError, TypeError, json.JSONDecodeError) as e:\n        print(f\"Proof verification failed: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 1\n====\ndef _cli_verify_proof(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Handle the 'verify-proof' subcommand.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        with open(args.proof_file, \"r\") as f:\n            proof = json.load(f)\n        chain = VerificationChain.load_json(args.chain_file)\n        root_str = None\n        if args.root is not None:\n            root_str = args.root if args.root.startswith(\"sha256:\") else f\"sha256:{args.root}\"\n        valid = chain.verify_inclusion_proof(proof, root_str)\n    except (KeyError, ValueError, TypeError, json.JSONDecodeError) as e:\n        print(f\"Proof verification failed: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 1\n>>>>\nThis requires CLI schema changes: add chain_file as a positional argument to verify-proof and optionally --epoch-index to prove-record. No further architectural issue remains once proofs are anchored to stored epochs."
