      "DESCRIPTION": "run_immune_pipeline() contaminates the active v1 synthesis path with observation-only shadow/v2 verdicts, so baseline decisions are no longer attributable to the intended primary pipeline. This goes deeper than prior reports about shadow leakage because the code explicitly comments that some components are still 'for comparison logging only', yet all verdicts from CT v2, B-Cell v2, and other active/shadow cells are appended into the single all_verdicts list before helper_t_cell_synthesize(). Evidence: in bench/immune_agents.py, Stage 2 collects cytotoxic_t, ct_v2, b_cell, b_cell_v2, nk_v2 into all_verdicts; then helper_t_cell_synthesize(triaged, all_verdicts) consumes that merged list. helper_t_cell_synthesize deduplicates only by CellType, not by tool_used or pipeline generation, so for CellType.CYTOTOXIC_T and CellType.B_CELL it keeps only the highest-confidence verdict per cell type. That means CT v2 (tool_used='ct_v2_falsifier', confidence up to 0.90/0.95) can overwrite CT v1 mechanical verdicts (tool_used='ct_mechanical', confidence often <= 1.0 * verification_rate), and B-Cell v2 can overwrite B-Cell v1, even before reconciliation. This violates the stated staged architecture and makes the later reconciliation gate partly meaningless because v1 is already polluted by v2 inputs.",
      "PROPOSED_FIX": "Split verdict collection into explicit v1_active_verdicts and v2_shadow_verdicts; feed helper_t_cell_synthesize() only the active v1 set and helper_t_v2_shadow() only the v2-aware set, then reconcile.",
      "VERIFIED": true,
      "FIND": "Location: bench/immune_agents.py, function run_immune_pipeline(), Stage 2 collection and Stage 3 synthesis. The code does:\n- all_verdicts = []\n- extends all_verdicts with results from cytotoxic_t, ct_v2, b_cell, b_cell_v2, nk_v2\n- calls helper_t_cell_synthesize(triaged, all_verdicts)\n- calls helper_t_v2_shadow(triaged, all_verdicts)\nThis is structurally wrong because helper_t_cell_synthesize() is documented as the v1 synthesis path, while ct_v2/b_cell_v2 are documented elsewhere as comparison/shadow or architectural improvements. Since helper_t_cell_synthesize() deduplicates by CellType only, not by tool_used, it cannot distinguish CT v1 from CT v2 or B-Cell v1 from B-Cell v2. Therefore the active decision path is contaminated.",
      "FIX": "<<<<\n    # ── Stage 2: Parallel verification (WP6a: v2 components active) ──\n    all_verdicts: List[CellVerdict] = []\n    t0 = time.monotonic()\n\n    # MF-20 fix: deep-copy triaged list for NK to prevent race conditions\n    import copy\n    triaged_for_nk = copy.deepcopy(triaged)\n\n    with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=6) as pool:\n        futures = {}\n\n        # 2a: CT v1 (code FFF investigation)\n        if ct_enabled:\n            futures[\"cytotoxic_t\"] = pool.submit(\n                cytotoxic_t_cell, triaged, source_paths, ct_timeout,\n            )\n\n        # 2a': CT v2 falsifier (WP6a: now ACTIVE, verdicts feed pipeline)\n        if ct_enabled:\n            futures[\"ct_v2\"] = pool.submit(\n                cytotoxic_t_cell_v2_shadow, triaged, source_paths, ct_timeout,\n            )\n\n        # 2b: B-Cell v1 (SymPy + z3 + stats — still primary for non-AST claims)\n        futures[\"b_cell\"] = pool.submit(b_cell_verify, triaged)\n\n        # 2b': B-Cell v2 AST-grounded z3 (WP6a: now ACTIVE)\n        futures[\"b_cell_v2\"] = pool.submit(\n            b_cell_v2_shadow, triaged, source_paths,\n        )\n\n        # 2c: NK v2 (WP6a: now PRIMARY — FP continue fix + intra-round dedup)\n        futures[\"nk_v2\"] = pool.submit(\n            nk_cell_v2_shadow, triaged_for_nk, prior_findings, tau_sim,\n            false_positive_db,\n        )\n\n        # Collect results — all active cells feed all_verdicts\n        for name, future in futures.items():\n            try:\n                result = future.result(timeout=ct_timeout + 30)\n                if name == \"nk_v2\":\n                    # NK v2 returns (triaged, verdicts) tuple\n                    _, nk_verdicts = result\n                    all_verdicts.extend(nk_verdicts)\n                    for v in nk_verdicts:\n                        tool_usage[v.tool_used] = tool_usage.get(v.tool_used, 0) + 1\n                else:\n                    cell_verdicts = result\n                    all_verdicts.extend(cell_verdicts)\n                    for v in cell_verdicts:\n                        tool_usage[v.tool_used] = tool_usage.get(v.tool_used, 0) + 1\n            except Exception as e:\n                # Cell failure is non-fatal — log and continue\n                import logging\n                logging.getLogger(__name__).warning(\n                    \"Immune cell %s failed: %s: %s\", name, type(e).__name__, e\n                )\n====\n    # ── Stage 2: Parallel verification ─────────────────────────────────\n    v1_active_verdicts: List[CellVerdict] = []\n    v2_verdicts: List[CellVerdict] = []\n    all_verdicts: List[CellVerdict] = []\n    t0 = time.monotonic()\n\n    # MF-20 fix: deep-copy triaged list for NK to prevent race conditions\n    import copy\n    triaged_for_nk = copy.deepcopy(triaged)\n\n    with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=6) as pool:\n        futures = {}\n\n        if ct_enabled:\n            futures[\"cytotoxic_t\"] = pool.submit(\n                cytotoxic_t_cell, triaged, source_paths, ct_timeout,\n            )\n            futures[\"ct_v2\"] = pool.submit(\n                cytotoxic_t_cell_v2_shadow, triaged, source_paths, ct_timeout,\n            )\n\n        futures[\"b_cell\"] = pool.submit(b_cell_verify, triaged)\n        futures[\"b_cell_v2\"] = pool.submit(\n            b_cell_v2_shadow, triaged, source_paths,\n        )\n        futures[\"nk_v2\"] = pool.submit(\n            nk_cell_v2_shadow, triaged_for_nk, prior_findings, tau_sim,\n            false_positive_db,\n        )\n\n        for name, future in futures.items():\n            try:\n                result = future.result(timeout=ct_timeout + 30)\n                if name == \"nk_v2\":\n                    _, nk_verdicts = result\n                    v1_active_verdicts.extend(nk_verdicts)\n                    v2_verdicts.extend(nk_verdicts)\n                    all_verdicts.extend(nk_verdicts)\n                    for v in nk_verdicts:\n                        tool_usage[v.tool_used] = tool_usage.get(v.tool_used, 0) + 1\n                else:\n                    cell_verdicts = result\n                    all_verdicts.extend(cell_verdicts)\n                    if name in (\"cytotoxic_t\", \"b_cell\"):\n                        v1_active_verdicts.extend(cell_verdicts)\n                    if name in (\"ct_v2\", \"b_cell_v2\"):\n                        v2_verdicts.extend(cell_verdicts)\n                    for v in cell_verdicts:\n                        tool_usage[v.tool_used] = tool_usage.get(v.tool_used, 0) + 1\n            except Exception as e:\n                import logging\n                logging.getLogger(__name__).warning(\n                    \"Immune cell %s failed: %s: %s\", name, type(e).__name__, e\n                )\n>>>>",
      "FOLLOW": "Stage 3 must be updated to use the split lists. Exact downstream replacements required:\n<<<<\n    final_verdicts, final_confidences = helper_t_cell_synthesize(triaged, all_verdicts)\n====\n    final_verdicts, final_confidences = helper_t_cell_synthesize(\n        triaged, v1_active_verdicts,\n    )\n>>>>\nand\n<<<<\n    v2_final, v2_conf = helper_t_v2_shadow(triaged, all_verdicts)\n====\n    v2_final, v2_conf = helper_t_v2_shadow(\n        triaged, v2_verdicts + v1_active_verdicts,\n    )\n>>>>\nThis preserves full per-finding observability in ImmuneResponse.cell_verdicts by still returning all_verdicts grouped later, while restoring semantic separation between v1 synthesis and v2 synthesis. It also exposes a second issue: helper_t_cell_synthesize() still deduplicates by CellType only, which remains acceptable for v1_active_verdicts but would have been invalid for mixed-generation inputs."
    },
