      "FLAW_CLASS": 1,
      "ABSTRACTION_INDEX": 0.68,
      "DESCRIPTION": "The skin barrier active-mode comment and return contract are inconsistent with implementation, creating a semantic trap for callers and future maintainers. skin_barrier_check() is documented and coded to return '(all_findings, barrier_results) — findings unchanged in shadow mode', but run_immune_pipeline() labels Stage 0 'now ACTIVE' and then ignores the returned passed_findings variable entirely, recomputing filtering from barrier_results. This is not just cosmetic duplication: the API of skin_barrier_check() no longer communicates whether it returns filtered or unfiltered findings, and the local variable name passed_findings is false in active mode because the function currently always returns the original findings list. That makes the stage interface misleading and easy to misuse in other callers.",
      "PROPOSED_FIX": "Make skin_barrier_check() return the actually passed findings list deterministically, in both modes; make run_immune_pipeline() use that returned list rather than re-deriving barrier filtering.",
      "VERIFIED": true,
      "FIND": "Location: bench/immune_agents.py, functions skin_barrier_check() and run_immune_pipeline(). Evidence:\n- skin_barrier_check() docstring says returns all_findings unchanged in shadow mode.\n- The function always returns findings, results regardless of pass/fail.\n- run_immune_pipeline() assigns passed_findings, barrier_results = skin_barrier_check(...), then ignores passed_findings and recomputes failed_ids/barrier_filtered/barrier_rejected.\n- Stage comment says active mode, but the stage interface still behaves like shadow mode. This split contract is error-prone.",
      "FIX": "<<<<\ndef skin_barrier_check(\n    findings: List[Finding],\n    source_paths: List[str],\n) -> Tuple[List[Finding], List[SkinBarrierResult]]:\n    \"\"\"Deterministic pre-filter: verify that cited code exists.\n\n    Checks each finding for file:line citations. If the cited code doesn't\n    exist at the cited location, the finding fails the barrier.\n\n    In shadow mode (Run 11), all findings pass through regardless.\n    The results are logged for observation.\n\n    Returns:\n        (all_findings, barrier_results) — findings unchanged in shadow mode\n    \"\"\"\n    results: List[SkinBarrierResult] = []\n    source_set = set(str(p) for p in source_paths)\n====\ndef skin_barrier_check(\n    findings: List[Finding],\n    source_paths: List[str],\n) -> Tuple[List[Finding], List[SkinBarrierResult]]:\n    \"\"\"Deterministic pre-filter: verify that cited code exists.\n\n    Checks each finding for file:line citations. If the cited code doesn't\n    exist at the cited location, the finding fails the barrier.\n\n    Returns:\n        (passed_findings, barrier_results) where passed_findings contains\n        only findings whose citations passed the barrier.\n    \"\"\"\n    results: List[SkinBarrierResult] = []\n    source_set = set(str(p) for p in source_paths)\n>>>>\nand at the end of the same function:\n<<<<\n    # Shadow mode: return all findings unchanged\n    return findings, results\n====\n    passed_ids = {r.finding_id for r in results if r.passed}\n    passed_findings = [f for f in findings if f.finding_id in passed_ids]\n    return passed_findings, results\n>>>>\nand in run_immune_pipeline():\n<<<<\n    passed_findings, barrier_results = skin_barrier_check(new_findings, source_paths)\n    timings[\"skin_barrier\"] = round(time.monotonic() - t0, 4)\n    tool_usage[\"skin_barrier\"] = sum(1 for r in barrier_results if not r.passed)\n\n    # WP6a: filter out findings that failed skin barrier (unless observation_only)\n    if not observation_only:\n        failed_ids = {r.finding_id for r in barrier_results if not r.passed}\n        barrier_filtered = [f for f in new_findings if f.finding_id not in failed_ids]\n        barrier_rejected = [f for f in new_findings if f.finding_id in failed_ids]\n        new_findings = barrier_filtered\n    else:\n        barrier_rejected = []\n====\n    passed_findings, barrier_results = skin_barrier_check(new_findings, source_paths)\n    timings[\"skin_barrier\"] = round(time.monotonic() - t0, 4)\n    tool_usage[\"skin_barrier\"] = sum(1 for r in barrier_results if not r.passed)\n\n    failed_ids = {r.finding_id for r in barrier_results if not r.passed}\n    barrier_rejected = [f for f in new_findings if f.finding_id in failed_ids]\n    if not observation_only:\n        new_findings = passed_findings\n>>>>",
      "FOLLOW": "This changes the interface contract of skin_barrier_check() for any external caller. In this artifact, only run_immune_pipeline() uses it, and the updated caller now consumes the returned passed_findings correctly. The logging comment about shadow mode in skin_barrier_check() should be removed or relocated because observation_only is controlled by run_immune_pipeline(), not by skin_barrier_check(). This fix also simplifies future application of the already-identified barrier accounting fixes because Stage 0 now has a coherent data flow."
    },
