      "FINDING_ID": "R6_F005",
      "SEVERITY": 0.77,
      "FLAW_CLASS": 6,
      "ABSTRACTION_INDEX": 0.57,
      "DESCRIPTION": "InsectBrain.compute_metrics() writes metrics into self.state.round_records[round_idx] and reads findings_this_round from self.state.all_findings[round_idx], implicitly assuming round_idx is a dense zero-based positional index. That assumption is not guaranteed by the public API: persist(round_idx, ...) accepts any integer and appends records/findings in call order. If rounds are skipped, replayed, or resumed with non-dense numbering, metrics are written to the wrong record or omitted. Evidence: persist() appends record to round_records and appends findings to all_findings, regardless of round_idx value; compute_metrics() indexes those arrays by round_idx rather than searching for matching record.round_idx.",
      "PROPOSED_FIX": "Stop treating round_idx as a list index; locate the matching RoundRecord by record.round_idx, and compute findings_this_round from the matching record rather than list position.",
      "VERIFIED": true,
      "FIND": "Location: bench/insect_brain.py, function compute_metrics(). The code uses:\n- if round_idx < len(self.state.all_findings): metrics['findings_this_round'] = len(self.state.all_findings[round_idx])\n- if round_idx < len(self.state.round_records): self.state.round_records[round_idx].metrics = metrics\nBut persist() only appends, so these arrays are ordered-by-arrival, not keyed-by-round_idx. Any non-dense or recovered schedule breaks this positional logic.",
      "FIX": "<<<<\n        # Totals\n        metrics[\"total_findings\"] = float(\n            sum(len(rnd) for rnd in self.state.all_findings)\n        )\n        if round_idx < len(self.state.all_findings):\n            metrics[\"findings_this_round\"] = float(\n                len(self.state.all_findings[round_idx])\n            )\n        else:\n            metrics[\"findings_this_round\"] = 0.0\n\n        # Update the round record with metrics if it exists\n        if round_idx < len(self.state.round_records):\n            self.state.round_records[round_idx].metrics = metrics\n====\n        # Totals\n        metrics[\"total_findings\"] = float(\n            sum(len(rnd) for rnd in self.state.all_findings)\n        )\n        matching_record = next(\n            (r for r in self.state.round_records if r.round_idx == round_idx),\n            None,\n        )\n        if matching_record is not None:\n            metrics[\"findings_this_round\"] = float(matching_record.finding_count)\n            matching_record.metrics = metrics\n        else:\n            metrics[\"findings_this_round\"] = 0.0\n>>>>",
      "FOLLOW": "This fix removes the hidden requirement that round_idx be positional. It also reveals a checkpoint gap: load_checkpoint() restores all_findings but not round_records, so after recovery compute_metrics() will report findings_this_round=0.0 until fresh RoundRecords are recreated. That is a separate persistence incompleteness issue not previously fixed here; if recovery is expected to support metrics on historical rounds, checkpoint load/save must persist enough round record metadata."
    },
