      "ABSTRACTION_INDEX": 0.62,
      "DESCRIPTION": "_verify_search_manifest() gives verification credit for any syntactically valid regex in Grep steps, without checking that the grep step targets the reviewed source set. This is the grep analogue of the already-identified read-path scoping bug, and it matters because CT v2 confidence is partly derived from verified manifest step count. Evidence: for tools in ('Grep','grep','rg'), the function converts args to a string, compiles it as regex, and increments verified. It does not inspect whether args include a path, whether that path is under source_paths, or even whether the command shape is plausible. A manifest step like {'tool':'grep','args':'foo'} gets full credit as a 'verified search operation' despite not referencing any file.",
      "PROPOSED_FIX": "Require grep/rg manifest args to resolve to at least one in-scope source path, and only then count the step as verified.",
      "VERIFIED": true,
      "FIND": "Location: bench/immune_agents.py, function _verify_search_manifest(). Read steps were partly scoped, but Grep steps remain unscoped. Since cytotoxic_t_cell_v2_shadow() sets test_severity = man_verified and maps confidence using test_severity, this bug directly inflates confidence for unverifiable search manifests.",
      "FIX": "<<<<\n        elif tool in (\"Grep\", \"grep\", \"rg\"):\n            # Check pattern is valid regex\n            pattern = args if isinstance(args, str) else str(args)\n            try:\n                re.compile(pattern)\n                verified += 1  # Pattern is at least syntactically valid\n            except re.error:\n                issues.append(f\"Invalid grep pattern: {pattern}\")\n====\n        elif tool in (\"Grep\", \"grep\", \"rg\"):\n            grep_arg = args if isinstance(args, str) else str(args)\n            try:\n                re.compile(grep_arg)\n            except re.error:\n                issues.append(f\"Invalid grep pattern: {grep_arg}\")\n                continue\n\n            matched_scope = False\n            for sp_path in source_paths:\n                sp_str = str(sp_path)\n                if sp_str in grep_arg or os.path.basename(sp_str) in grep_arg:\n                    matched_scope = True\n                    break\n\n            if matched_scope:\n                verified += 1\n            else:\n                issues.append(\n                    f\"Grep step not scoped to source set: {grep_arg}\"\n                )\n>>>>",
      "FOLLOW": "cytotoxic_t_cell_v2_shadow() uses man_verified to set test_severity and confidence. After this fix, manifests with regex-only or out-of-scope grep claims will earn less confidence, which is the intended effect. This also exposes a structural limitation: args is an untyped free-form string, so scope validation is heuristic. A stronger downstream fix would normalize manifest entries to structured fields such as pattern and path."
    },
    {
      "FINDING_ID": "R6_F007",
      "SEVERITY": 0.69,
      "FLAW_CLASS": 4,
      "ABSTRACTION_INDEX": 0.66,
      "DESCRIPTION": "Checkpoint persistence in InsectBrain is incomplete for the documented recovery contract: load_checkpoint() restores all_findings and convergence flags, but it does not restore round_records, failures, durations, timestamps, immune responses, or per-round metrics. This means read_context(), relay_conversational(), signal_complete(), and compute_metrics() operate on an empty or partial in-memory history after recovery, despite checkpoint load logging success. Evidence: _save_checkpoint() stores only completed_round/timestamp/all_findings/active_models/converged/convergence_reason. load_checkpoint() reconstructs only all_findings and a few scalar state fields; round_records remains empty.",
      "PROPOSED_FIX": "Persist a minimal serialized round_records list in checkpoint and restore it in load_checkpoint().",
      "VERIFIED": true,
