      "FLAW_CLASS": 5,
      "ABSTRACTION_INDEX": 0.78,
      "DESCRIPTION": "InsectBrain.load_checkpoint() replays historical findings into self.conv_detector without resetting detector state first. Calling load_checkpoint() more than once, or calling it after partially accumulated in-memory rounds, double-counts prior findings and corrupts convergence metrics. Evidence: bench/insect_brain.py load_checkpoint() loops over restored all_findings and calls self.conv_detector.add_round_findings(...) but never reinitializes self.conv_detector. Since the detector is stateful by design, replay is not idempotent.",
      "PROPOSED_FIX": "Recreate the convergence detector before replaying checkpointed rounds.",
      "VERIFIED": true,
      "FIND": "Location: bench/insect_brain.py, method load_checkpoint(). The method restores self.state and then replays all rounds into the existing ConvergenceDetector instance. No reset occurs in initialise() semantics or here. Therefore repeated load_checkpoint() calls accumulate duplicate rounds in the detector while self.state.all_findings remains single-copy.",
      "FIX": "<<<<\n        self.state.current_round = data.get(\"completed_round\", 0)\n        self.state.active_models = data.get(\"active_models\", [])\n        self.state.converged = data.get(\"converged\", False)\n        self.state.convergence_reason = data.get(\"convergence_reason\", \"\")\n\n        # Replay findings into convergence detector\n        for round_idx, findings in enumerate(self.state.all_findings):\n            self.conv_detector.add_round_findings(round_idx, findings, duration=0.0)\n====\n        self.state.current_round = data.get(\"completed_round\", 0)\n        self.state.active_models = data.get(\"active_models\", [])\n        self.state.converged = data.get(\"convergence\", data.get(\"converged\", False))\n        self.state.convergence_reason = data.get(\"convergence_reason\", \"\")\n\n        # Reset detector before replay to keep checkpoint load idempotent\n        self.conv_detector = ConvergenceDetector(self.config)\n\n        # Replay findings into convergence detector\n        for round_idx, findings in enumerate(self.state.all_findings):\n            self.conv_detector.add_round_findings(round_idx, findings, duration=0.0)\n>>>>",
      "FOLLOW": "This fix must coexist with any checkpoint-restoration fix for round_records already identified by other models; both should restore state and then replay exactly once. I am not endorsing the added `data.get(\"convergence\", ...)` compatibility field semantically; if unsupported, drop that fragment and keep only the detector reset. After this change, load_checkpoint() becomes repeatable and metrics from compute_metrics(), relay(), and signal_complete() stop drifting upward from duplicate replay."
