      "DESCRIPTION": "run_immune_pipeline() silently accepts and processes duplicate finding_id values, causing verdict conflation across distinct findings. Evidence: almost every downstream structure is keyed only by finding_id: barrier failed_ids set, verdicts_by_finding dict, final_verdicts/final_confidences dict, and reconciliation maps. If two Finding objects share the same finding_id, one finding's cell verdicts can overwrite or merge with the other's, barrier filtering can remove both together, and the returned ImmuneResponse no longer represents one-to-one findings. No uniqueness check exists at pipeline ingress.",
