      "DESCRIPTION": "skin_barrier_check() extracts only the first citation from a finding and passes the finding if that one citation resolves, even when later citations in the same description are nonexistent or out of range. Evidence: citations are collected by regex, then the code explicitly says `# Check first citation (most findings cite one location)` and ignores the rest. A multi-citation finding claiming evidence from A:10 and B:9999 therefore passes if A:10 exists, despite part of the asserted evidence being false. For a barrier whose purpose is hallucination filtering, partial citation validation is unsound.",
