    "DESCRIPTION": "FIND: `bench/immune_agents.py`, function `_verify_ct_claim()`, exact-match branch in the snippet verification block. The code currently treats either `snippet_normalised in actual_normalised` or `actual_normalised in snippet_normalised` as a 1.0-confidence 'Exact match at line N'. That is not an exact match. Because `code_snippet` is allowed to contain 1–5 lines, a fabricated multiline snippet that merely embeds the true cited line will satisfy `actual_normalised in snippet_normalised` and be scored as exact. Evidence from the implementation: `actual_line = lines[line_num - 1].strip()`, `snippet = evidence.get(\"code_snippet\", \"\").strip()`, then the branch uses symmetric substring containment instead of equality on the cited line. This overstates evidence quality and can upgrade partially hallucinated CT evidence to full-confidence support.",
